# The three homepages (root, es, zh) canonicalize to a bare trailing slash
# (see R/build_hreflang.R), but Quarto still writes and links to index.html
# with no redirect enforcing that, so Google was indexing /index.html as a
# separate, non-canonical duplicate of /. Force (!) is required here because
# these paths exactly match real files in public/, which Netlify would
# otherwise serve directly instead of applying the redirect.
/index.html / 301!
/es/index.html /es/ 301!
/zh/index.html /zh/ 301!

# The GSC coverage report (Alternate page with proper canonical tag) also
# showed Google crawling individual research/software/teaching pages without
# their .html extension -- external sites link to them that way, but Quarto
# only ever emits the .html file, so the bare path served the same content
# with a canonical tag pointing elsewhere instead of just redirecting there.
# These don't need force: nothing on disk exists at the extensionless path.
/research/:slug /research/:slug.html 301
/software/:slug /software/:slug.html 301
/research /research.html 301
/software /software.html 301
/talks /talks.html 301
/teaching /teaching.html 301
/people /people.html 301
